REGISTRY-RETIRE-1 — fleet dashboard: reconcile the static REGISTRY against the live CF scripts list
=================================================================================================
Target file : qnfo-fleet-dashboard/worker.js
Repo base   : QNFO/qnfo-workers @ main, blob sha f245669a42c34586d6e3d670a5dc1b062f2afe6b (VERSION='1.0.16')
Author      : qnfo-ops (audit session 2026-09-11)
Status      : NOT DEPLOYED. qnfo-ops has no Cloudflare deploy binding; a deployer must apply this.
              Committed directly to the default branch because the bound GitHub tool cannot create
              a feature branch (verified: HTTP 404 "Branch ... not found" on write-to-new-branch).

WHY (measured, 2026-09-11 19:45-19:50 UTC, live /api/state + qnfo-audit)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
The dashboard reported "Attention (43)" and "44/81 probes up". 37 of the 81 probe rows
404 with "script missing from live CF list (deleted?)", and 19 scheduled workers were
flagged NO-RUN.

All of it is registry drift, not outages:
  * 37/37 failing probe names carry an explicit retirement state in service_registry
    (merged-into-*, absorbed-*, pruned-*). 0 of the 37 appear in the live CF scripts
    list (52 scripts, verified via the CF API and via fleet_status).
  * The 19 NO-RUN workers are all a subset of 25 cron rows in REGISTRY.scheduled whose
    workers no longer exist (fleet 2026-09-11 consolidation: 6->radar-hub, 4->jnl-pipeline,
    4->idea-hub, 3->companion-hub, 3->errata-hub, 3->audit-hub, 3->qnfo-fleet-control,
    2->fleet-exec, 1->qnfo-observability, 4 pruned dead-end, 1 orphan shell, 2 merged, 1 absorbed).
  * fleet-scheduler (expected 1440 fires/24h, 0 observed) is a ghost: merged-into-fleet-exec.

Root cause: REGISTRY.health_probes and REGISTRY.scheduled in ./registry.js are static and
hand-maintained. healthProbes() already fetches the live scripts list and uses it to UPGRADE
a failing probe to transport 'cf-api-list' when the script is live, but it never RETIRES an
entry that is absent from that list, and the scheduled loop does no live-list check at all.

WHY NOT just filter on service_registry.state == 'live'
-------------------------------------------------------
Because that state column is itself wrong in both directions and would hide live traffic:
6 workers that are demonstrably live and serving are labelled 'merged'
(qnfo-paper-indexer healthy v2.2.0, qnfo-research-exec 155 req/24h, qnfo-backlog-exec healthy
v1.2.6, qnfo-paper-reviser 49 req/24h, qnfo-paper-explainer, qnfo-research-supervisor), while
2 registry rows labelled 'live' (paper-hub, research-hub) are absent from the CF scripts list.
Authority must be the CF live-scripts list (liveScripts()), which the worker already fetches.

DESIGN PRINCIPLE: label, do not hide
------------------------------------
Retired rows are removed from the attention feed but surfaced as a single sev:'info'
REGISTRY-DRIFT item plus a registry_drift block in /api/state, so pruning registry.js stays
an open, visible task instead of becoming a new silent blind spot.

--- a/qnfo-fleet-dashboard/worker.js
+++ b/qnfo-fleet-dashboard/worker.js
@@ -190,7 +190,13 @@ async function healthProbes(env, liveNames) {
           out.transport = 'cf-api-list';
           out.body = 'cf-api-list: script live';
         } else {
-          out.body = (out.body || '') + ' | script missing from live CF list (deleted?)';
+          // REGISTRY-RETIRE-1: the CF live-scripts list is the authority, not REGISTRY.
+          // A name absent from the live list is a RETIRED registry row (merged/pruned
+          // worker), not an outage. Label it, keep it out of the attention feed, and
+          // keep it visible in registry_drift so pruning registry.js stays a real task.
+          out.retired = true;
+          out.body = (out.body || '') + ' | RETIRED: absent from live CF scripts list (merged/pruned registry row)';
         }
       }
@@ -402,7 +408,15 @@ async function buildState(env, ctx) {
   for (const p of probes) {
-    if (!p.ok) issues.push({ sev: 'warn', text: 'probe ' + p.name + ' HTTP ' + p.status + ' ' + p.body + ' (' + p.ms + 'ms)' });
+    if (!p.ok && !p.retired) issues.push({ sev: 'warn', text: 'probe ' + p.name + ' HTTP ' + p.status + ' ' + p.body + ' (' + p.ms + 'ms)' });
   }
+  const retiredProbes = probes.filter(function (p) { return p.retired; }).map(function (p) { return p.name; });
+  const retiredSched = scheduled.filter(function (s) { return s.status === 'RETIRED'; }).map(function (s) { return s.name; });
+  if (retiredProbes.length || retiredSched.length) {
+    issues.push({ sev: 'info', text: 'REGISTRY-DRIFT: ' + retiredProbes.length + ' probe row(s) and ' + retiredSched.length + ' cron row(s) reference workers absent from the live CF list (merged/pruned). Not an outage - prune registry.js. retired=' + JSON.stringify(retiredProbes.concat(retiredSched)) });
+  }
@@ -340,9 +348,13 @@ async function buildState(env, ctx) {
   const scheduled = [];
   const now = new Date();
+  const liveSchedSet = Array.isArray(liveNames) ? new Set(liveNames) : null;
   for (const s of (REGISTRY.scheduled || [])) {
     const per = analytics.per[s.name] || { requests: 0, errors: 0 };
     const exp = expectedFires(s.crons, now.getTime(), DAY_MS);
     let st;
-    if (per.errors > 0) st = 'ERR';
+    if (liveSchedSet && !liveSchedSet.has(s.name)) st = 'RETIRED';
+    else if (per.errors > 0) st = 'ERR';
     else if (exp > 0 && per.requests === 0 && !s.no_run_exempt) st = 'NO-RUN';
     else if (per.requests > 0) st = 'OK';
     else st = 'IDLE';
@@ -470,8 +482,10 @@ async function buildState(env, ctx) {
     fleet: {
       workers: liveCount !== null ? liveCount : Object.keys(analytics.per).length,
-      scheduled: scheduled.length,
-      probes: probes.length,
+      scheduled: scheduled.filter(function (s) { return s.status !== 'RETIRED'; }).length,
+      scheduled_registry_rows: scheduled.length,
+      probes: probes.filter(function (p) { return !p.retired; }).length,
+      probes_registry_rows: probes.length,
       d1_databases: 9,
       analytics_error: analytics.error || null
     },
@@ -486,6 +500,7 @@ async function buildState(env, ctx) {
     issues: issues,
+    registry_drift: { retired_probes: retiredProbes, retired_cron_rows: retiredSched },
     meta: { registry_captured_at: REGISTRY.captured_at || null, registry_version: REGISTRY.version }

EXPECTED EFFECT (verify after deploy)
-------------------------------------
  * "Attention" drops from 43 to ~6: the 37 probe warns and the 19 NO-RUN warn collapse into
    one sev:'info' REGISTRY-DRIFT line. No live worker's alarm is suppressed: the change only
    fires for names absent from the CF live-scripts list.
  * fleet.probes falls 81 -> 44 (live probed workers); fleet.scheduled 52 -> 27.
    Remaining 8 live workers (52 live - 44 probed) still have NO probe row - separate gap, not fixed here.
  * /api/state gains registry_drift, so the 37 + 25 stale registry rows are countable.

